--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0160 / PR #395 added the `claude-code-cli` route adapter
(`query_claude_cli` in `src/aedist/harness.py`) and wired it into the
legacy / manual entry point `src/aedist/query_direct.py`. End-to-end
smoke against `query_direct.py --model claude-sonnet-4-6-cli` works.

The job-board worker (`src/aedist/worker.py`) was NOT updated. Its
`_query_and_save` calls `query_model(client, ...)` unconditionally,
and `query_model` only dispatches between Ollama-native and
OpenAI-compatible — there is no branch for `claude-code-cli`. A worker
asked to process a job whose model has `route: claude-code-cli` would
either NPE (the route's client is `None`) or fall through to the
OpenAI path with a None client.

The example sweep added in PR #395 (`[sweeps.sweep_smoke_claude_cli]`
in `experiments/experiments.toml`) goes through `manager generate` →
worker drain. As written it would silently fail at worker runtime.
This is documented inline (the docstring of `query_claude_cli` says
"not suitable for controlled sweeps") but the registry + sweep
plumbing doesn't prevent the misconfiguration.

## Scope

Two reasonable resolutions:

1. **Wire the route through the worker too.** Mirror the
   `query_direct.py` change: in `_query_and_save`, detect
   `model_entry.get("route") == "claude-code-cli"`, call
   `query_claude_cli(model_id, messages)`, bill from `result["cost_usd"]`.
   Skip `compute_cost` (registry prices are 0.0 — would silently bill 0).

2. **Fail fast.** Add an assertion early in worker dispatch that rejects
   the route with a clear message pointing at `query_direct.py`. Cheaper
   to implement, harder to use.

(1) is the right answer if any user wants to run multi-rep cli sweeps
with budget tracking via the job board. (2) is enough if the route is
purely for capability checks via `query_direct.py`.

Note: the same gap exists for the direct adapters (`anthropic`,
`openai-responses`, `mistral-agents`, `qwen-dashscope`) — they all live
outside the worker too. So this gap is consistent with the existing
class of "direct adapters bypass the worker". The fix should either be
done across the class (worker learns to dispatch on `route` and call
the right per-route module) or scoped to just the `claude-code-cli`
case if the direct-adapter exclusion is intentional.

## Actions (option 1)

1. In `src/aedist/worker.py::_query_and_save`, before calling
   `query_model`, branch on `model_entry.get("route") == "claude-code-cli"`.
2. Call `query_claude_cli(model_id, messages, timeout=job.timeout_seconds)`.
3. Compute `cost = float(result.get("cost_usd") or 0.0)` instead of
   `compute_cost(usage, model_entry)`.
4. Record `provider_order = None` (no OpenRouter routing on this path)
   and any other extra_body-derived fields as None.
5. Add an integration test under `tests/test_worker.py` (or similar):
   mock the CLI subprocess, drive a one-job drain, assert `done/` has 1
   file and `cost_usd` came from the mock JSON.

## Actions (option 2)

1. In `src/aedist/worker.py::_query_and_save`, raise
   `NotImplementedError` if `model_entry.get("route") == "claude-code-cli"`
   with a message pointing at `query_direct.py`.
2. Update `experiments/experiments.toml`'s
   `[sweeps.sweep_smoke_claude_cli]` comment to flag it as
   `query_direct.py`-only.

## Test

Adherence: a test that loads every `route` value referenced in
`experiments/models.yaml` and asserts the worker either handles it
or refuses with a clear error.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Either: worker dispatches `claude-code-cli` correctly (option 1),
      OR: worker raises a clear `NotImplementedError` (option 2).
- [ ] Example sweep in `experiments.toml` documents the path that
      actually works.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
